@slow
Feature: Look for cross site scripting (xss) using wapiti against scanme.nmap.org

Scenario: Using wapiti, look for cross site scripting and verify no issues are found
  Given "wapiti" is installed in my path
  And the following profile:
     | name                | value                         |
     | url                 | http://scanme.nmap.org        |
  When I launch a "generic" attack with:
  """
  wapiti -u <url> -m xss -d 1 --scope folder -f txt -o /dev/stdout
  """
  Then the output should contain "Reflected Cross Site Scripting :   0"
  And the output should contain "Stored Cross Site Scripting :   0"
